@@s045 last row, the closest to 1000
@@s046 last row, the maximum
@@s047 The table is the same as for the knapsack: each row is computed by looking only at the row above, with the option "I do not add" and the option "I add a piece". Only the labels change.
@@s048 Trap: double slopes
@@s049 Two slopes between the same points can have different scores (sample 2: 1→2 with score 2 and 1→2 with score 4). If you store them in a matrix <code>voto[u][v]</code>, the second overwrites the first and you keep the last one read, not the best. With a list of arcs (from, to, cost) all the slopes remain, and the <code>max</code> chooses.
